NEAT moth pursuit
=================
Train a drone controller to pursue recorded moth trajectories using NEAT.
Run these commands from the project root in PowerShell with Python 3.12.

Setup
-----
    python -m venv .venv
    .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt

Training
--------
    .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m script.main

Models are saved in neat_models/. Settings are in config and src/config/.
Add --generations 2 for a short run.

Repeat a saved model's training settings:
    .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m script.main --from-model "neat_models/MODEL_DIRECTORY"

Replay
------
    .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m script.replay "neat_models/MODEL_DIRECTORY"

Omit the directory to replay the newest complete model.

Datasets
--------
Training uses moth_dataset/moth_train_dataset.npz.
Final evaluation uses moth_dataset/moth_eval_dataset.npz.

Reproduce the supplied datasets using the same original raw CSV files:
    .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m src.tools.moth_dataset --source "PATH_TO_RAW_CSV_FOLDER" --split legacy --eval-ratio 0.16 --output-dir "dataset_reproduction" --no-plots

For new datasets, use --split recording to keep each source recording entirely
in training or evaluation. This is the default split.

Sweeps and reports
------------------
Run the full sweep (3 baselines and 60 sensitivity runs, 100 generations each):
    .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m script.sweeps.main

Generate evaluation results and baseline flight plots:
    .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m src.evaluation.main

Outputs go to results/. Reports use the newest complete model per setting and
seed (10, 20, 30), and require the full 100-generation sweep protocol.
